<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Miguel Barbachano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1806">1806</a>–<a href="/years/1859">1859</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Miguel Barbachano y Tarrazo was a politician from Mérida who served several times as governor of Yucatán between 1841 and 1853. His rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago-mendez">Santiago Méndez</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a> dominated the peninsula's politics. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">Caste</a> War he negotiated Yucatán's reunion with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1848 in exchange for military aid against the Maya rebels.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/miguel-barbachano.jpg" alt="Miguel Barbachano" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giggette · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Miguel_Barbachano_Lito.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
